dudix@nepomuk.gerwin.net (Michael Duda) writes:
>I have a problem with /dev/lp0.
>I can send printjobs to the queue but thats all.

Solution:

lprsetup adds the tag :rw: to /etc/printcap.  This doesn't work
for /dev/lp0.  Remove it, restart the daemon, have fun.


>If I install a printer on the serial interface (/dev/tty00 or
>/dev/tty01) there is no problem.

There would have been once you decided to print a big PS file :-)

>I can also send a string to the
>parallel interface and it works: "echo hallo > /dev/lp0"

We went here through precisely the same procedure.  Amusingly, in 
dxbook it says:

|             Note
| The DEC OSF/1 Operating System does not support
| parallel printers.

This ranks very high in my "Best quotes" list.


Greetings, Michael
