Then they *definitely* shouldn't support a seperate /usr.  This sounds
like an out and out bug (and before people attack sgi, yes, I know that
tcsh requires /usr, if you have it as the root shell; that's why we
put comments in the relnotes that you shouldn't do that, unless you
have /usr as part of the root filesystem).
