>Maybe running Xdec with -dpi0 100? (Seems illogical though, as
>sizer talks with the kernel, right, and not with Xdec?)

All AlphaStations with the "ZLXp" series cards are capable of
1280x1024 resolution given the correct monitor. I think out of
the box the ZLXp is setup for 1024x764. The ZLXp manual gives you
the switch settings for various resolutions and frequencies that
are supported. The four switches are on the graphics card and are
accessible from the back of the system. The first thing I do on
a new 200 is to turn all switches to face up and then turn on the
system which provides 1280x1024 and 72Hz.

