I call a system UNIX if I don't have to drop out of the UNIX API based
environment to perform system management and administration functions.

It doesn't much matter if the details are different, since so long as
it's under the UNIX flag I can still write scripts to cover the differences.

It's not that admin is so valuable, either, it's just that it's a good
test case. Admin is so basic to the system, so if you need to pop back
to some other environment for that odds are you're going to have to do it
elsewhere as well.
