>	We are having problems in setting up dialup modem
>	connection between two alphas. The workstations are
>	DEC AXP 3000/300X model, and the modems are V.32bis
>	with V.42bis, dialback and RTS/CTS hardware flow
>	control configured on. The cables between modems and
>	alphas are 25-pin flat cable with compressed D25
>	connectors; all needed RS-232 signals are sure connected.
>	DTE speed between modems and alphas is set to 38400bps
>	at both ends. OS is DEC OSF1 3.0.
>
    The System Settings seem to be ok. Be sure that you desabled the XON/XOFF
    handshake if you are using RTS/CTS.

>	All works perfectly, *except* flow control. When I
>	try to upload/download anything with kermit, all I get
>	is timeouts and too many retries. If I type 'cat' in
>	shell, and try to copy/paste a 60-char line from
>	another xterm, the line will be garbled. The serial
>	ports and/or OS on alpha seems to not handle 38400bps
>	serial rate very well.

    The seriel port is connected to a modern Zylog UART Chip, who accept
    a transfer rate up to 1 MBps. This cannot cause the problem.
    OSF/1 Ver 3.0 handles baudrates correct up to 38400 Bps. This I tested
    with a AXP 3000-500 on a ISDN TA.

    To check your configuration, you can use the stty command
	stty < /dev/ttyXX
    and set the parameters at your need.

    The problem could be that you are using at both side not the same
    modem type. Also if the V.. standard should be a standard, there is
    possible that the modems fail.

    There are also a few modems (e.g. I had problems with Zyxel), that don't
    function properly under UNIX

