  You could have been a bit more specific about the modem. I am using
USR v.34 modems (28k) under OSF. Here is briefly what I do:

1. Set up the modem:
   -- with dip switches: disable local echo, result codes; enable auto answer
   -- with kermit (tip, etc. will bark about 38400 baud not being supported)
      I connect to the port (/dev/tty00), and do a at&f1&w. This is a hw
      flow control, FIXED DTE SPEED (!) setup. I could get the same
      on a Telebit T3000 (aka worldblazer 14.4) with some Sregister settings.

2. Set up /etc/gettydefs (1 line):

38400NP# B38400 OPOST ONLCR TAB3 IGNPAR IXON IXANY ISTRIP ECHO ECHOE ECHOK ISIG 
CS8 CREAD HUPCL CLOCAL # B38400 OPOST ONLCR SANE TAB3 IGNPAR IXON IXANY ISTRIP E
CHO ECHOE ECHOK ISIG CS8 CREAD HUPCL #Login: #38400NP

3. Modify /etc/inittab:

dialup:23:respawn:/usr/sbin/getty -h    /dev/tty00 38400NP vt100

4. init q

  No matter what the negotiated connection speed is, the machine and
the modem uses 38k. No hacking with autobaud, etc....

Enjoy,
  Gyula
