So what ?

If you have essentially single user workstations, and the disk fills up,
that is tough for that particular user, who usually has only himself or
herself to blame. And most often even those who are not very computer
literate will understand the problem and will be able to deal with it.

If you are running multi-user machines, where one silly mistake can make 
the life difficult for many people, and you think it is below your dignity
to devise a repartitioning strategy, you deserve every problem you get.
It is not really on to think that leaving everything as it was pre-installed 
will probably work well enough. This is exactly why computers were not
pre-installed in mainframe days, and why (entry level) machines are
pre-installed now.

