buxduac@zippy.dct.ac.uk writes:

>System: Dec Alpha 3000/400
>OS:  Osf1 V1.2
>Problem,
>
>I am trying to add a Exabyte 8505 Tape drive to this system, I have tried the
>following:
>
>%./MAKEDEV /dev/rmt13
>MAKEDEV: special file(s) for /dev/rmt13: 
>MAKEDEV: unknown device in: /dev/rmt13
>
>which didn't work. 13 is the correct SCSI number for the device.
>
>Any Ideas what the correct procedure is ?

  First off, you need to make sure that there is a controller and device
entry in your /sys/conf/SYSTEMNAME file. You should have the following
entries:

controller      asc1       at tcds0     slot  1 vector    ascintr

  followed by:

device tape             tz13    at asc1         drive 104

Note that the order is important: The controller definition MUST precede
the device definition.

  Rebuild the kernel, install and reboot

  cd /dev

  MAKEDEV tz13

  et voila!

  Piece of free advice: UPGRADE!! OSF/1 v1.2 is ANCIENT! We've just
begun shipping v3.2 yesterday, and there are THOUSANDS of bug fixes
since 1.2!!! ZILLIONS maybe :)

