>I recently set up the Post Office Protocol Daemon (popd) on our
>OSF/1 system.  It works great using PC Eudora as a client on the 
>PC end.
>
>The question I have is, now that all mail is delivered to the PC's
>how can users still have the abilty to dial in from home and get
>their mail too?
>
>Is there a way to send mail to user@pop and the regular mail spool
>file in /usr/spool/mail/user?
>
Ron;

  Just create a .forward file in each user's home directory with the 
following entries:

	\username, username.pop

  This will send mail to both spoolers. Note that the backslash character
is required, it's not a typo!

