> Are you sure that your modem is set right?

	I have a straight flat calbe between the Alpha and the modem.
	I have also setup RTS/CTS flow control on at the modem.

	Actually, I managed to get a bearable connection when I enable
	XON/XOFF between Alphas and modems, between modems (rarely needed)
	and issue stty ixon ixoff on Alpha shell. I could even transfer
	some files with zmodem. I think xon/xoff sucks, but this the best
	I could manage to set up.

	I even tried to set up RTS/CTS flags on the tty with my own
	tiny C program, since the OSF stty knows absolutely nothing
	about RTS/CTS. I wonder why?

	Anyway, here's my program:

--- 8< ---

/*
 *	myrtscts.c
 *
 *	This source code is in public domain.
 *	You may do whatever you want with it.
 */


#include	<stdio.h>
#include	<termios.h>


void	usage(const char *progname)
{
    fprintf(stderr, "Usage: %s [on|off]\n", progname);
}


int	main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
    struct termios tp;


    memset(&tp, 0, sizeof(struct termios));
    if (tcgetattr(0, &tp))
    {
	perror("tcgetattr");
	exit(1);
    }

    switch(argc)
    {
    case	1:
	fprintf(stderr, "RTS/CTS %s\n",
		tp.c_cflag & CRTSCTS ? "on" : "off");
	exit(0);

    case	2:
	if (!strcmp(argv[1], "on"))
	    tp.c_cflag |= CRTSCTS;
	else
	    if (!strcmp(argv[1], "off"))
		tp.c_cflag &= ~CRTSCTS;
	    else
	    {
		usage(argv[0]);
		exit(-1);
	    }
	if (tcsetattr(0, TCSANOW, &tp))
	{
	    perror("tcsetattr");
	    exit(1);
	}
	exit(0);

    default:
	usage(argv[0]);
	exit(-1);
    }

    return 0;
}
--- 8< ---

