Mark-

I'm pretty much doing the same thing you're doing; however, I don't
suspend kermit, I exit completely (^\c, then exit).  Then do a
nohup slattach /dev/tty00 38400 &.  One thing we ran into is that
it is a good idea to ^d out of the process that initiated the slattach,
as doing a ^c (as in to get out of the ping you're testing with) will kill
slattach.

The only other thing we do is a route add default (slip address).  I
don't know if you're running routed, or if you do or don't want to have
hard-coded routes, but those are some of the problems we ran into.

