>System: Dec Alpha 3000/400
>OS:  Osf1 V1.2
>Problem,
>
>I am trying to add a Exabyte 8505 Tape drive to this system, I have tried the
>following:
>
>%./MAKEDEV /dev/rmt13
>MAKEDEV: special file(s) for /dev/rmt13: 
>MAKEDEV: unknown device in: /dev/rmt13
>
>which didn't work. 13 is the correct SCSI number for the device.
>
>Any Ideas what the correct procedure is ?
>
>Andy C
>Sys Admin
>Microcentre
>University of Dundee
>Dundee
>.

try this:
# cd /dev
# ./MAKEDEV tz13
#
This generates al the {n}rmt?{l,n,a,h} device entries in the /dev drectories.

Make sure you see this device tz13 at boot time and you should have no 
problem accessing it.


