In article <3hb11d$ld4@sgi.iunet.it>, walter@rtb.saclantc.nato.int (Walter Zimmer) writes:
>How do I change the Default Visual of my screen?
>Any help is appreciated
>
>Thank you very much
>Walter Zimmer		walter@saclantc.nato.int
>

In the file /usr/lib/X11/Xserver.conf, uncomment the args section and add 
arguments so it reads
args <
	-vclass0 TrueColor
>
for example if your screen#0 has 24bits. See also 'man Xdec' for more 
arguments!

