In article <3i1hei$jd2@spool.mu.edu>, stevax@vinny.csd.mu.edu (Peter L. Buschman) writes:
> I'm sure this problem has an utterly simple fix, but I'm at a loss.
> I'm trying to program using the curses library. Under a VMS system,
> the following program compiles just fine, but on the OSF/1 system, 
> I get linker errors.
> 
> Can anyone help me with this?
> 
> The program is: (minimal curses program)
> 
> : #include <curses.h>
> : 
> : main()
> : {
> :   initscr();
> :   box(stdscr,'%','%');
> :   refresh();
> : }
> 
> And when compiling, the errors are:
> 
> : ld:
> : Unresolved:
> : initscr
> : box
> : stdscr
> : wrefresh

You need to include the 'curses' when you link evertyhing together.

Use the following on your 'cc' command:

    cc prog.c -o prog -lcurses

This causes the 'loader' to look for external references into
libcurses.a

Read the MAN page on cc for more info.

