In article <3i0qpf$71r@physics.esu3.k12.ne.us>, jkirkpat@physics.esu3.k12.ne.us (Jake Kirkpatrick) writes:
|>I am trying to run CAP (Columbia Appletalk) on OSF/1 2.0.  I got everything
|>compiled, but when i try to run aarpd it needs the device name.  If i specify
|>ln0 it gives an error to the extent of no such file or directory.  I have 
|>checked for the existance of /dev/ln0, but its not there, or anything else
|>that even would remotely match.  Does anyone have any ideas on what I am 
|>should use for the device name?  Thanks,

You need to make the packetfilter devices:

# cd /dev
# ./MAKEDEV pfilt

You may also need to rebuild your kernel if you didn't build it with
packetfilter support.  (to do that, edit /sys/conf/FOO where FOO is
your system name all capitalized.  Add the line

options		PACKETFILTER

to the file.  Then issue the command "doconfig -c FOO" which will
rebuild the kernel.  Once it finishes, copy the new kernel to / and
reboot).
