Hello,

First, under the Dec Monitor, verify that your tape drive has been recognised :

   >> show device
   
   BOOTDEV     ADDR     DEVTYPE  DEVNAME
   
   dka0        a/0/0 disk     rz25
   dka100      a/1/0 disk     rz25
   dka200      a/2/0 disk     rz58
-> mka300      a/3/0 tape     exb-820
   dka400      a/4/0 rodisk   rrd42
   mka600      a/6/0 tape     tz30

Then compute the logical number for the /dev file. Just apply the
following formula :

   Logical number = BudId * 8 + TargetId

For the example above, we have : 0 * 8 + 3  = 3

Then create the /dev file :

   # cd /dev
   # MAKEDEV tz?     (For the example above tz3)

The system will create the files rmt?{a,l,m,h} and the associated
nrmt?{a,l,m,h}.

You can find additional information in the manual pages of :
   SCSI(7), mtio(7) and tz(7)

Vincent Masquelier
(Vincent.Masquelier@crpht.lu)


