]
] It's possible I'm doing something that doesn't work with osf's implementation
] of rstat.  For example, the clntudp_create call takes a rpc program and
] and version number (RSTATPROG and RSTATVERS_TIME in my code).  You might
] verify that your osf rstat daemon is compatible.  You can use rpcinfo to check
] this, e.g.
]
]	rpcinfo -p <osfhost>
]	program vers    proto   port
]	...
]	100001  2       udp     1472    rstatd
]	100001  3       udp     1472    rstatd
]	100001  4       udp     1472    rstatd
]
] This shows that osfhost is using rpc program number 100001, and supports
] versions 2, 3 and 4 of the rstat protocol.  Then compare these numbers to
