In article <3hdghs$1hn@news.cs.tulane.edu>, pollard@tatanka.bmen.tulane.edu
(Dr. Andrew E. Pollard) writes:

|>We have a dual processor Alpha, but I can't figure out how to:
|>
|>	1. determine the processor I'm running my job on
|>	2. compile a FORTRAN code to run across both processors

DEC Fortran does not have built-in parallel processing support.  This is
provided by an optional product, KAP for DEC Fortran V2.0.  KAP will
examine your program for loops which can be safely run in parallel and
distribute them across an SMP system.

As another writer mentioned, you could also do your own manual decomposition
using the Posix threads package.
