Yes, yes, yes yes and some as add ons.

From what I've seen of Unix (HP/UX, DG/UX, AIX, and OSF/1), OSF/1 is
pretty much Unix.  The one thing I've noticed about the base OSF/1 is
that you have to buy an additional license (OSF-DEV) to run the
debugger.  I have no idea why you have to pay for this debugger (the
debugger on VMS is about a zillion times better and was free).
Go figure...

If you want detailed information on OSF/1 (or any other DEC products
hardware or software), the best place to look is on DEC's web servers.
You can start out at:

 www.digital.com

If you start there, and go to:

"Products and Services"
then "Software Product Descriptions"
then "DEC OSF/1"

you'll get to the Software Product Descriptions (SPDs).  The one for
