hejny@buntspecht.physik.uni-giessen.de (Volker Hejny) writes:


>In article <3g8mrv$37h@tenebris.rutgers.edu>, armhold@tenebris.rutgers.edu (George Armhold) writes:
>|>The OSF/1 3.0 rdump software does not support the remote host notation
>|>of user@machine:device.  It only supports machine:device.  Does anyone
>|>know of an rdump implementation that supports this?
>|>

>What does this implementation should do ? Normally, a dump of a device can 
>only be done by root. 

For security reasons, backups are often performed locally as root (so
root can access the entire filesystem) but are dumped to a remote tape
as another, non-privileged user.  

e.g.:

	rdump -f nobody@remote-host:/dev/nrst0 /usr

This will feed the bytes over the network to nobody@remote-host, which
has access to /dev/nrst0.

