Ricardo> Please, I'm trying to use a unix machine as x-terminal
Ricardo> of an osf machine (that is, "X -query osf.machine"). It
Ricardo> seems I need add some info to the protectec terminal
Ricardo> control database and/or to other places at the osf
Ricardo> side. Could anybody help me?

It depends on the X display name reported by xdm when it gets the
query.  If I remember correctly, xdm will use short names when
the two machines are in the same domain, and fully-qualified host
names otherwise.  Thus, if "NedsPC.Nashua.NH.US" and
"Alex.Hollis.NH.US" were both querying "Orb.Nashua.NH.US", then
it would see them as "NedsPC" and "Alex.Hollis.NH.US",
respectively.

Once you know what hostname you need to add, look at the entries
for "local:0" (which look like "local\:0") in the files
/etc/auth/system/ttys and /etc/auth/system/devassign.  Copy them,
changing the names as appropriate.

