Ray.Bellis@psy.ox.ac.uk (Ray Bellis) writes:

>Does anyone know if v3.2 of OSF/1 will support printing via the
>parallel port on suitably equipped machines?

I'll give my experience from V3.0 for it shows that documentation
and implementation sometimes differ:

quote from: "DEC  OSF/1 System  Administration, DEC OSF/1 Version  3.0"

|                        Note
|
|  DEC  OSF/1 Version  3.0 operating  system does
|  not support  parallel  printers.
|

Reading that and finding a Sub-D Parallel Printer port on the Back of
our 2100 AXP we were pretty amazed.  For a test, we did

	cat file > /dev/lp0

and it worked.  The following printcap entry allows access via lpd:

| lp3|3|post:\
|        :lf=/usr/adm/lpderrs:\
|        :xf=/usr/lbin/xf:\
|        :lp=/dev/lp0:\
|        :sd=/usr/spool/lp3:\
|        :mx#0:\
|        :pl#66:\
|        :pw#80:\
|        :sh:

Note that lprsetup(8) wants to add the :rw: tag during printer definition.
For the parallel interface to work correctly, this tag must be removed.

Hope it helps and works the same way with V3.2.

Michael
