Summary: How do we configure OSF/1 to run diskless without swapping?

We currently have an application which deserves a portable OSF/1 work
station running multimedia software. The application is in a factory where
it is inconvenient to have to walk back to a central console containing the
work station, get the information and then walk back to the place where the
information is required. Since the system is diagnosing factory control
system problems, it is not possible to choose a convenient place to install
the system.

It occurred to me recently, as I was wheeling an AXP 3000-300X with its 19 inch
monitor around the factory, that the UPS that I was using was powerful
enough to keep the Alpha alive while it is moved near to where the problem
occurred. Because the factory floor is not smooth, I doubt that a spinning
disk drive would last long if it is subjected to the vibration that my
system was as I wheeled it around (I had the luxury of being able to power
the system down while I moved it - a luxury that the customer cannot afford
given that downtime costs them A$1000 a minute).

